UPSTREAM WORK
-------------

Accelerate Legal is a modified version of Mike, an open-source legal AI
platform:

    Mike — https://github.com/Open-Legal-Products/mike
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only.

Accelerate AI has modified that work, beginning in 2026. The modifications
include a rebrand from Mike to Accelerate Legal, a rebuilt design system and
information architecture, the Legal AI resources catalog, and the macOS desktop
application in `desktop/` together with the desktop authentication handoff it
depends on. Everything else — the Next.js web application, the Express backend,
the Word task-pane add-in, the database schema and migrations, the document
processing and LLM integration, and the deployment tooling — originates upstream
and remains substantially its work.

The system assistant and tabular-review workflows this application ingests are
maintained in a sibling catalog repository; upstream's is
<https://github.com/Open-Legal-Products/mike-workflows>.

Identifiers carrying the upstream product name are retained deliberately, not
by oversight: the legacy session cookie, the credential-encryption salts, the
export manifest signing context, the Word document-settings keys, and the
workflow front-matter namespace are all read under their pre-rename spellings so
that data created by an upstream deployment keeps working after an upgrade. See
the initial commit message and `backend/src/lib/authSession.ts` for the full
list.


BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
---------------------------

Legal AI resources catalog
    `backend/src/lib/resources/legalAiResources.json` and its copy under
    `frontend/src/app/components/resources/` are generated from
